<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vasai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vasai, formerly Bassein, is a town on the coast north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Mumbai</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Ceded by Bahadur Shah of the Gujarat Sultanate to the Portuguese in 1534, it became an important fortified city of Portuguese India until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> captured it in 1739. The Treaty of Bassein of 1802 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> and the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> was signed there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vasai.jpg" alt="Vasai" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oknitop. Transferred to Commons by Carlos Luis M C da Cruz. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vasaifort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
